---
title: Parmesan Baked Parsnips
description: One of the nicest ways to serve parsnips, baked crisp and golden-brown with a Parmesan coating
servings: 8
course: Side
locale: en_GB
prep time: 20m
cook time: 45m
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: British
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- savoury
- side-dish
- british
---

Combine the @plain flour{175%g}, @parmesan cheese{50%g}(freshly grated), @salt and @black pepper{}(freshly ground) in a mixing bowl.

Peel the @parsnips{1.25%kg} using a potato peeler. Halve and quarter lengthways, and cut each length into half across. Cut out some of the woody centres.

Put the parsnips in a saucepan, cover with boiling water and add salt. Boil for ~{3%minutes}.

Drain the parsnips and while still steaming coat with the flour and Parmesan mixture a few at a time. Transfer to a large kitchen tray. This needs to be done quickly; the mixture will only coat them while they are still steamy.

Place a solid roasting tin in the oven with sufficient @groundnut oil{} to cover the base and add @butter{1%knob}. Pre-heat the oven to 180°C.

When the oven is ready remove the tin and place over low direct heat. Using tongs place the parsnips side-by-side in the tin. Tilt and baste all the parsnips with the hot fat. Bake for ~{20%minutes}.

Turn the parsnips over. Drain off any surplus fat. Bake for a further 15 to ~{20%minutes} until crisp and golden.